From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 01:09:42 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] ui-egui: simplified Slides toolbar, one row of our own
 instead of the ribbon

office_toolbar.rs draws one row of the controls people use most (new slide, layout, font, size,
B/I/U, colour, bullets, numbering, alignment, text box, picture, shapes, table, transliterate,
version history) instead of ribbon::show, with a button that switches to the full ribbon; in the
full ribbon mode a "Simple ribbon" pill floats over the right end of the tab row. The web build
always shows the row. Icons are the vendored Fluent UI System Icons (MIT), drawn through
craft_ui::icons::SvgIconSet and egui_extras' SVG loader. Labels go through the catalogs, so the row
is translated with the rest of the UI.

The upstream edits are the mod line and a three-line branch at the ribbon call site in lib.rs,
layout_menu made pub(crate), and the office_overlay helpers for the shared toolbar setting.
Tests (office_toolbar_tests.rs): every command id still exists, the row shows the designed
controls and acts, the two buttons switch modes, the pill clears the tabs at 1024 px.
